From: Medium1992 <122653016+Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:23:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 103/105] XHTTP: Take upstream's h2Params as the base of the
 server's HTTP/2 config

Upstream's XHTTP h2Params (XTLS/Xray-core#7295) took field 30 of the
splithttp Config. h2Flow moves to 102, in the fork-owned 100+ block, as in
Jolymmiles/Xray-core; a protobuf config built against 32 must be
regenerated, JSON configs are unaffected.

On the server h2Params is the base HTTP/2 config: a receive window set in
h2Flow overrides it, and with the governor on its defaults fill a window
neither sets. A governed server rejects MaxConcurrentStreams above the
streams the governor tracks. h2Params is parsed before the listener binds,
so a bad value leaves no listener behind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
